    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      244.39,
      281.23,
      366.67,
      290.3
    ],
    "text": "STATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECT",
    "fonts": [
      "Times,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      143.47,
      301.27,
      455.54,
      340.7
    ],
    "text": "Clause 2 : This clause amends section 4 of the Minimum Wages (Indian Labour)Ordinance (Chapter 135) (hereinafter referred to as the \u201cprincipal enactment\u201d) and thelegal effect of the section as amended is to increase the employable age of children onestates.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      143.47,
      351.67,
      455.5,
      381.02
    ],
    "text": "Clause 3 : This clause amends section 11 of the principal enactment and legal effect ofthe section as amended is to extend the liability of any employer in respect of issuingmonthly allowance of rice.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      143.47,
      391.99,
      455.5,
      421.34
    ],
    "text": "Clause 4 : This clause amends section 18 of the principal enactment and legal effect ofthe section as amended is to increase the age limit of female labourers in respect ofpayment of minimum rates of wages.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
